#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the launch profile's agent-model qualification battery (Appendix A).

Three suites against the pinned hosted deployment (AG-01, TDD-3.1.37): 100
real five-tool/schema conversations with at least 99 valid complete
submissions and no successful forbidden tool; 50 preserved figure/table
questions with at least 80% correct; 100 evidence-location questions
balanced over early/middle/late positions in 16k/32k/64k contexts with at
least 90% correct at each length. The model is declared with the five
production tool schemas and every call it makes is parsed by the same strict
parsers the tool service uses; the answers come from a fixture dispatcher
over a small synthetic corpus (per the fixture population documented under
tests/qualification/inference/fixtures/). The model itself is the real
pinned endpoint, reached through the production transport and counted with
the pinned processor's tokenizer, unless --dry-run is given. Reads the
provider key from the environment only, reserves worst-case spend against
the day/month caps before each conversation, records every request/response
by hash, and writes an immutable report to docs/evidence/inference-capacity/.

No paid execution happens without an explicit --endpoint, --processor-dir
and a populated provider key; --dry-run exercises the same mechanism against
a scripted in-process transport and a word-count stand-in for the processor,
and writes a clearly labeled report instead.
"""

